WEBVTT

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.360
For the first time in human history,

00:00:31.402 --> 00:00:34.072
we share a global commons,

00:00:34.072 --> 00:00:36.908
where, irrespective of where we are
in the physical world,

00:00:36.949 --> 00:00:40.119
we can convene
and share information freely.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.790
Most people at that time
couldn't see what it meant

00:00:43.831 --> 00:00:46.167
to be connected by
a network of computers.

00:00:46.709 --> 00:00:51.798
In fact, many people thought
the internet itself was a scam or a fad.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.885
But a few early internet pioneers
saw the potential

00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:57.678
in this burgeoning technology.

00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:02.725
One of those early internet pioneers,
John Perry Barlow,